+Keep one authoritative board per event. Editors submit commands over HTTPS; browsers display a revisioned view of the board. A self-hosted WebSocket service delivers committed revisions to connected browsers with low latency, without coupling the board to a realtime vendor.
 
-Delivery, change storage, and browser recovery must be designed together after this choice. Polling would favor cursor queries; self-hosted sockets would need connection management and replay; hosted delivery would need publication reconciliation and provider credentials. Neither operating cost nor minimum operational burden has been declared the overriding criterion.
+Delivery, change storage, and browser recovery are designed together. The change store retains replayable event revisions and reliably publishes committed revisions to delivery. Delivery owns WebSocket connection capacity and session management. Browsers reconnect after transport failures and catch up from their last applied revision before resuming live updates.
 
